# build.py --check compares viewer.html byte-for-byte against src/ + vendor/, so
# line endings must not depend on which platform ran the checkout. Without this,
# a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true can rewrite LF to CRLF inconsistently
# between the generated file and its sources, and the build check fails for
# reasons that have nothing to do with the change under test.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The vendored three.js build is one 607 KB line. Never let any tool touch it.
vendor/three.min.js -text -diff
